    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Gaiseric took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> without a fight in 439, while most of its people were at the races in the hippodrome, and styled himself King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and Alans.</li><li>The kingdom's fleet looted the coasts of both Roman empires for decades, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 455 and destroyed a combined imperial fleet at Cape Bon in 468 with fire ships.</li><li>The Vandal kings were Arian Christians: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huneric">Huneric</a> exiled almost 5,000 Nicene clergy into the desert and in 483 ordered every Nicene church closed and its property confiscated.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The best Vandal warriors ended their days as five cavalry regiments, the Vandali Iustiniani, on the Persian frontier of the empire that had destroyed their kingdom.</p></aside>
    </section>

